    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0435" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v14p1/pg407"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">790.5/2–2454: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 184<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        the Republic of China</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-04-08T18:58:00-05:00">April 8, 1954—6:58
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>823. Your 358<anchor n="1" xml:id="d184-f1"/> and 476.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d184-f2"/> Department has decided not take any action before Geneva
                    Conference with respect to proposed bilateral mutual security treaty with
                    Chinese Government. Available time for necessary careful consideration of matter
                    with key Congressional leaders is insufficient. Decision is without prejudice to
                    later consideration of question.</p>
                <pb facs="0436" n="408" xml:id="pg408"/>
                <p>Robertson informed Chinese Ambassador to this effect April 7.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d184-f3"/> You are authorized communicate decision to Foreign
                    Minister.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
